initialize-tmpdir-before-process-startup

Lane: normalization

FlatPatch: initialize-tmpdir-before-process-startup

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Ensure and publish a canonical temporary root before normal process startup creates worker threads.

Requires: none

Provides: After specialized helper dispatch and native dotenv loading, preserve a nonempty TMPDIR override or remove an empty override and select the standard-library host temporary root; create and canonicalize the selected directory, propagate errors, and publish TMPDIR before alias preparation.

Boundary: Home and harness selection, component-specific staging, and sandbox temporary-directory policy remain separate responsibilities; specialized helper invocations retain their early dispatch.

Verification: arg0 normal_dispatch_normalizes_empty_tmpdir_before_alias_setup checks process and dotenv empty overrides at the actual alias startup boundary; home-dir ensure_tmpdir_creates_selected_override verifies directory creation and canonical paths.


